                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6cae1028-cc11-3a32-8c34-e2fba03c741e",
                        "entry_id": "c4048fc7-5871-3e55-a2ba-631d1dbe0ba0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "физиол., устар. инфекционное заболевание, вызываемое находящимися в почве микробами и выржающееся в резких судорогах мышц; столбняк"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "560a8188-a84f-4075-a7e7-409eb7f00eca",
                                "sense_id": "6cae1028-cc11-3a32-8c34-e2fba03c741e",
                                "text": "По Ландуа и Марей требуется от 300 до 440 раздражений в секунду, чтобы привести в состояние тетануса мышцы крыльев насекомых."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf98458b-cd20-4893-86fa-dbc5c305a106",
                                "sense_id": "6cae1028-cc11-3a32-8c34-e2fba03c741e",
                                "text": "Вообще признаётся, что с усилением раздражения высота тетануса нарастает до известной границы, а с ослаблением раздражения она падает до нуля."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ffbef11e-afbb-4415-9934-72266d7adf83",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4048fc7-5871-3e55-a2ba-631d1dbe0ba0",
                        "source_sense_id": "6cae1028-cc11-3a32-8c34-e2fba03c741e",
                        "target_lang_word": "tetanus",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tetanus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33c69696-469a-3647-a604-5d24f3e11387",
                                        "entry_id": "a7d3f5aa-6f58-357d-9ed6-934ebd3bfff8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A serious and often fatal disease caused by the infection of an open wound with the anaerobic bacterium Clostridium tetani, found in soil and the intestines and faeces of animals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57461bb3-9871-4fea-a49c-1b9d7eb24d87",
                                                "sense_id": "33c69696-469a-3647-a604-5d24f3e11387",
                                                "text": "Compared to 290 children with TQQ negative, CWDs were significantly less likely to receive antenatal care (P=0.003), to get a maternal tetanus shot during antenatal care (P=0.004) and to receive full vaccination (P=0.01)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1bd0ded-255f-3caf-acf3-f395e3b35fe6",
                                        "entry_id": "a7d3f5aa-6f58-357d-9ed6-934ebd3bfff8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state of muscle tension caused by sustained contraction arising from a rapid series of nerve impulses which do not allow the muscle to relax."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1435bf2a-7276-4466-9330-cafcd56e5d51",
                                                "sense_id": "c1bd0ded-255f-3caf-acf3-f395e3b35fe6",
                                                "text": "We first saturated LTP in one pathway by applying repetitive tetani that had no effect on the control pathway […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
